<div class="content">

  <div class="abstract">
    <span class="abstract-label">Abstract</span>
    GUES v0.2 corrects a foundational error in v0.1. The original claim that information flow is the primary substrate is replaced by the stronger claim that constraint structure is primary, with distinction, information, causality, geometry, and gauge freedom all emerging in that order. Taking a constraint system K = (X, A) as given — where X is possible configurations and A is admissible transitions — we derive the emergence ladder, propose that Standard Model gauge groups are automorphisms of the constraint structure, and argue that E8 is best understood as a fixed point of coarse-graining flows over constraint algebras rather than as a source of physics. The black hole expansion mechanism from v0.1 is formally frozen pending compilation of the lower ladder. Three Charter-grade null hypotheses are formalized. This paper is explicitly labeled E1.
  </div>

