  <section id="competing">
    <h2>8 · Competing Explanations</h2>

    <div class="competing">
      <div class="competing-title">GR + ΛCDM as sufficient</div>
      <p>The null hypothesis. Spacetime is fundamental. The Standard Model forces are irreducibly distinct. Dark energy is vacuum energy. This fits all current data. GUES must derive predictions that differ from ΛCDM — not merely reframe them.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="competing">
      <div class="competing-title">String Theory / M-Theory</div>
      <p>Forces unified geometrically via compactified dimensions. Calabi-Yau manifolds as the ambient object. The constraint-first framework must specify how it differs. In particular: does Aut(K) reduce to known string-theoretic structures in appropriate limits?</p>
    </div>

    <div class="competing">
      <div class="competing-title">Verlinde Entropic Gravity</div>
      <p>Gravity already emergent from entropy without requiring the other forces to follow. The constraint-first framework subsumes Verlinde — entropy is compressed distinction, derived from constraint — but must specify what it predicts beyond Verlinde.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="competing">
      <div class="competing-title">The universe is federated, not unified</div>
      <p>The most structurally dangerous competing explanation. The Standard Model may emerge from one constraint structure, spacetime from another. Their observed relationships may be consistency conditions rather than common ancestry. GUES must identify why a unified constraint system is more parsimonious than a federated one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <section id="nulls">
    <h2>9 · Formal Falsification Structure</h2>
    <p>Three Charter-grade null hypotheses, formalized from adversarial review:</p>

    <div class="null-hyp">
      <span class="null-label">Null Hypothesis 1 — Non-Uniqueness</span>
      <p><strong>Claim:</strong> A unique constraint structure underlies the observed gauge physics.</p>
      <p><strong>Null:</strong> There exist K₁ ≠ K₂ such that O(K₁) = O(K₂) within current measurement precision, where O denotes all admissible observables.</p>
      <p><strong>Rejection threshold:</strong> If two inequivalent constraint structures reproduce all claimed observables, the uniqueness claim fails and G loses explanatory necessity.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="null-hyp">
      <span class="null-label">Null Hypothesis 2 — Generic Emergence</span>
      <p><strong>Claim:</strong> Observed gauge structure requires the proposed constraint hierarchy.</p>
      <p><strong>Null:</strong> Randomly sampled constraint systems generate equivalent gauge structures with frequency p > p_crit, where p_crit = 0.05 is set before sampling.</p>
      <p><strong>Rejection threshold:</strong> If gauge structure emerges generically from arbitrary constraint systems, GUES provides no explanatory advantage over a null model.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="null-hyp">
      <span class="null-label">Null Hypothesis 3 — Information Primacy Failure</span>
      <p><strong>Claim:</strong> Information is derived from constraints and cannot be defined prior to distinction.</p>
      <p><strong>Null:</strong> A mathematically coherent formal system exists satisfying all three conditions: (1) information is defined, (2) no distinguishable states exist, (3) no hidden constraints are present.</p>
      <p><strong>Rejection threshold:</strong> If such a system exists, the constraint-first hierarchy fails at its first rung and the entire framework requires reconstruction.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <section id="openquestions">
    <h2>10 · Open Questions</h2>

    <div class="open-questions">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Compile the first rung:</strong> Demonstrate that Constraint → Distinction without importing graph theory, information theory, or geometry as hidden assumptions. If this step is contaminated, the entire ladder is contaminated.</li>
        <li><strong>Compute Aut(K):</strong> For a well-defined candidate constraint system, compute the automorphism group and identify whether it contains the Standard Model gauge groups as stabilizer subgroups.</li>
        <li><strong>Define F:</strong> Specify the coarse-graining flow over constraint algebras and demonstrate that E8 is a fixed point or attractor under that flow.</li>
        <li><strong>Derive uniquely:</strong> Show that the constraint system K uniquely yields SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1) as its low-energy automorphism structure. Not embed it. Not accommodate it. Derive it uniquely.</li>
        <li><strong>Unfreeze black holes:</strong> Characterize what a black hole does to the constraint system in its vicinity. This is the prerequisite for any claim about expansion.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <section id="conclusion">
    <h2>11 · Conclusion</h2>
    <p>GUES v0.2 is a better conjecture than v0.1 because it was broken by people who knew what they were doing and rebuilt from the failure.</p>
    <p>The primitive object is a constraint system. Everything else — distinction, information, causality, geometry, gauge freedom — emerges from it in a specific order. The Standard Model gauge groups are automorphisms of the constraint structure. E8 is a fixed point of coarse-graining flows. The black hole expansion mechanism is frozen until the lower ladder compiles.</p>
    <p>This is still E1. Nothing here is proven. But the conjecture is now structured around a foundation that does not collapse at its first rung, and its failure modes are named, formal, and testable in principle.</p>

    <div class="conclusion-block">
      This is an educated guess.<br>
      The acronym is intentional.<br>
      The revision is the point.
    </div>

